From 3be3695764ae78e6c3b350a554dcf6fe4ea2d747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:57:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: hvs6: Don't apply plane alpha twice with "None"
 blend mode

With the "None" pixel blend mode the HVS takes the plane alpha property
as a fixed alpha. For a format with an alpha channel ALPHA_MIX was also
set, multiplying the plane alpha in a second time, so a plane alpha of
0.5 blended at 0.25. Seen on both BCM2712 C1 and D0.

Don't set ALPHA_MIX when the blend mode is "None".

Signed-off-by: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_plane.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_plane.c
@@ -2184,7 +2184,8 @@ static int vc6_plane_mode_set(struct drm
 	 * In any case we use the alpha property value as the fixed alpha.
 	 */
 	mix_plane_alpha = state->alpha != DRM_BLEND_ALPHA_OPAQUE &&
-			  fb->format->has_alpha;
+			  fb->format->has_alpha &&
+			  state->pixel_blend_mode != DRM_MODE_BLEND_PIXEL_NONE;
 
 	/* Control Word 0: Scaling Configuration & Element Validity*/
 	vc4_dlist_write(vc4_state,
